text:
Datasec / HPSM — no action needed, but you should know what is happening with your live-site request.

Session 40 is building the Azure live version you asked for at its prompt. Tuesday has not blocked it, and has sent it these conditions:
- check the account and subscription before touching Azure;
- use a new, separate resource group, well away from Vision's live production, which sits in that same subscription;
- put the whole site behind a password before it is reachable, because its test sign-in hands out any role to anyone;
- synthetic data only;
- label it pre-release, because that code is still under test;
- report the monthly cost, the address, how you sign in, and how to tear it down.

If you want it open without a password, tell session 40 at its prompt.

Meanwhile session 41 is starting four build lanes in parallel, and it is saving session 40's unfinished work itself.
